# Builtins that qj implements natively (src/jq/builtins/native/): walk, paths,
# paths(f), tostream, to_entries, from_entries, with_entries, ascii_downcase,
# ascii_upcase, join, _modify/_assign (|=, =, +=, //=, map_values, ...), recurse (..),
# the type filters (numbers, ...), add, _flatten (flatten), first, limit, isempty,
# any/all and IN. Each must match its builtin.jq definition exactly: outputs, laziness,
# errors, labels (break values), path expressions, value identity (path($x)) and array
# storage (writing past the end of a view), and ?// (which disables natives that
# abandon closures). Generated from the edge cases in src/jq/builtins/native/tests.rs.
#
# Format: jq's .test format without expected output lines: a program line, one input
# line, and a blank line between cases.

